# Secrets
.env

# Collected/derived data — reproducible from collect.py + a token, so not versioned.
# Keep the directory structure via .gitkeep but ignore contents.
data/raw/*
data/processed/*
data/logs/*
data/*.log
data/predictions.jsonl
!data/**/.gitkeep

# Model artifacts. The three heads the deployed service actually loads
# (champion.joblib, category.joblib, dup_index.joblib -- ~34MB total, all
# well under GitHub's 100MB hard limit) ARE tracked: a plain `git push`
# drives Vercel's auto-deploy, which builds from the git tree, not the
# local filesystem, so anything the service needs at runtime has to be
# committed. The larger/unused heads (rf*.joblib, logreg*.joblib,
# effort.joblib -- retraining artifacts and an optional head Vercel drops
# for bundle size, see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md) stay out of git; rebuild them
# with `python -m ghic.train` or `python -m ghic.retrain`. The model/
# decision cards ARE tracked. reports/ is tracked too: the README links to
# the report and its figures.
models/*
!models/*.md
!models/champion.joblib
!models/category.joblib
!models/dup_index.joblib

# Local-only archive of course/personal files, not part of the published project
_archive/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

.vercel
.env*

# A separate project (its own git repo) that happens to live nested here on
# disk — not part of this repo.
/Elegant-Interface-Design/

# Installed via `npx skills add` at this directory by mistake (meant for the
# frontend project) — not relevant to this Python backend.
/.agents/
/skills-lock.json
